---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="6. Wire the box — AquaSense">
  <p class="kicker">Step 6 of 9</p>
  <h1>Wire the box</h1>
  <p class="lede">Gravity PH2.0 cables land on the screw-terminal breakout. Cable colors are DFRobot’s: red +, black −, blue analog. Highlight colors in the drawing are which probe. No custom PCB.</p>
  <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/wiring.svg`} alt="Gravity red black blue into screw terminals, then GPIO 32 34 39 18 16 17" style="margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--line)" />
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Order</th><th>Probe</th><th>Gravity wires</th><th>GPIO</th><th>Highlight</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1</td><td>SEN0169-V2 pH</td><td>blue A, red +, black −</td><td>32</td><td style="color:#1FA6A0">seagrass</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2</td><td>DFR0300-H EC</td><td>blue A, red +, black −</td><td>34</td><td style="color:#E6D5B8">sand</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3</td><td>SEN0237-A DO</td><td>blue A, red +, black −</td><td>39</td><td style="color:#C4452D">rust</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4</td><td>KIT0021 DS18B20</td><td>data / VCC / GND (kit pull-up)</td><td>18</td><td>foam</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5</td><td>MS5803-14BA</td><td>SDA / SCL / 3V3 / GND</td><td>16 / 17</td><td style="color:#7EB6D9">sky</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <ul>
    <li>Wiki pinout for SEN0169-V2: − GND, + VCC 3.3–5.5 V, A analog 0–3.0 V, BNC to the probe. <a href="https://wiki.dfrobot.com/sen0169-v2/">DFRobot</a></li>
    <li>Shared 3V3 and GND. Transmitters stay powered (no MOSFET).</li>
    <li>GPS SKU: GPIO 21/22 are GNSS UART. Do not use them as I2C.</li>
    <li>Do not jumper GPIO 4 or 5. Remove the microSD card before USB flash (GPIO 2).</li>
    <li>Optional carrier schematic (same nets): <code>hardware/kicad/</code>. Default is still this screw-terminal box.</li>
    <li>PG glands through the <em>bottom</em> of the Pelican. Silicone on threads.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">GPIO numbers: <a href="https://github.com/Xinyuan-LilyGO/LilyGo-Modem-Series/blob/main/docs/en/esp32/a7670-esp32/README.MD">LilyGO A7670 ESP32 README</a>. Same table in <code>hardware/pinmap.md</code> and <code>firmware/include/pins.h</code>. If a picture disagrees, the table wins.</p>
  <div class="checkpoint">
    <strong>Checkpoint.</strong> Inside the box: pH 32, EC 34, DO 39, temp 18, pressure 16/17. Five cables. No wires on 4 or 5.
  </div>
  <div class="pager">
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}build/calibrate/`}>← Calibrate</a>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}build/hull/`}>Next: build the hull →</a>
  </div>
</Base>
